// A consumer's definition whose parameter spelling a `use`d library's overload set ALREADY
// carries is a redefinition (`Disp-Key`, @PLN162) — the same refusal a single imported free
// function gives, and the one `shadows_a_method` gives a method.  Until this held, `hit(f:
// Fire)` beside `use overloadlib` registered in silence and a bare `hit(Fire {…})` answered
// the LIBRARY's body: two definitions of one signature, one of them unreachable and unwarned.
// The second cell is loft#788's standing refusal: a name two packages export bare must be
// called qualified, an overload set included.
// @ARGS: --lib tests/lib
// @falsified-at: 988288e7b — interpret exit 1 -> 0, interpret expectations FAIL/2 -> 0/2 (the suite's verdict, not a count of matches), native exit 1 -> 0, native expectations FAIL/2 -> 0/2 (the suite's verdict, not a count of matches)
// @falsified-by: tests/falsified/a-consumer-definition-of-a-carried-signature-is-a-redefinition.patch — interpret exit 1 -> 0, interpret expectations FAIL/2 -> 0/2 (the suite's verdict, not a count of matches), native exit 1 -> 0, native expectations FAIL/2 -> 0/2 (the suite's verdict, not a count of matches)
//   CHANNEL: expectations — on the control the first `@EXPECT_ERROR` is unmet (the consumer's
//   `hit(f: Fire)` registers in silence), so the suite's verdict is FAIL there and the file's
//   exit goes 1 -> 0 with it.  Not leak and not assert: a parse-time verdict.
//   ARMED: no instrument — the refusal is parse-time on either backend.
//   WITNESS: on the control the program compiles past the consumer's `hit` and a bare
